From 6426a515e042f32cb9f1d82ec9d0905e0c500d6c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rich Felker <dalias@aerifal.cx>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 16:26:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] strtod: fix incorrect logic detecting underflow

underflow should be reported (via ERANGE) on any inexact denormal
result, which is expressed in the logic as (denormal && frac). the
denormal boolean is set above based on the magnitude of the exponent
relative to the target type's exponent range after normalizing the
working mantissa to occupy LDBL_MANT_DIG bits directly above the radix
point. but, since rounding up can raise the exponent out of the
denormal range, there is additional logic to clear the denormal flag
when that happens, and it was wrong.

the logic clearing denormal triggered when:

    bits==LDBL_MANT_DIG+e2-emin

here e2+LDBL_MANT_DIG is the actual place of the highest bit, and
initially, bits+emin was equal to -emax+3. however, at the point the
condition is evaluated, bits no longer represents the full mantissa
width of the target type. it has already been replaced with a reduced
width corresponding to the precision of the denormal. as a consequence
of the replacement, the condition was basically always true (except
when bits gets clamped non-negative), and so the denormal flag got
cleared when rounding up with carry.

the logic is fixed by using the value -emax+3 which is constant for
the duration of the function, and by moving evaluation from before the
exponent adjust to after, since the denormal flag should be cleared
based on the new exponent, not the old exponent.

with this change, behavior has been confirmed to be correct for
rounding both up and down around the minimum normal and maximum
denormal double, expressed both as 21 decimal digits and the full
exact value.

this patch does not address missing underflow logic when parsing hex
floats, which is a separate issue.
---
 src/internal/floatscan.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/internal/floatscan.c b/src/internal/floatscan.c
index 2bc6830f..d1d388a2 100644
--- a/src/internal/floatscan.c
+++ b/src/internal/floatscan.c
@@ -299,10 +299,9 @@ static long double decfloat(FILE *f, int c, int bits, int emin, int sign, int po
 
 	if ((e2+LDBL_MANT_DIG & INT_MAX) > emax-5) {
 		if (fabsl(y) >= 2/LDBL_EPSILON) {
-			if (denormal && bits==LDBL_MANT_DIG+e2-emin)
-				denormal = 0;
 			y *= 0.5;
 			e2++;
+			if (e2+LDBL_MANT_DIG >= -emax+3) denormal = 0;
 		}
 		if (e2+LDBL_MANT_DIG>emax || (denormal && frac))
 			errno = ERANGE;
-- 
2.55.0

